{"id":"NCT06994377","title":"Emotional Distress in Patients With Metastatic Breast Cancer in First Line of Therapy","official":"The Impact of Emotional Distress on First Line Therapy in Patients With Metastatic Breast Cancer (EIRENE): a Prospective Observational Study","summary":"Few data about the impact of emotional distress (ED) on treatment efficacy in patients with metastatic breast cancer (mBC) are available.\n\nAim of this study is to assess the outcomes of patients with mBC receiving first-line treatment according to the presence of baseline ED.","conditions":["Metastatic Breast Cancer"],"interventions":[{"type":"BEHAVIORAL","name":"ED and quality of life assessment"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Age over 18 years\n* Confirmed histological diagnosis of breast cancer\n* No prior treatment for advanced/metastatic cancer\n* Indication to receive first-line therapy as per standard clinical practice based on the disease subtype:\n\n  1. cohort A (HR-/HER2-, PD-L1+): pembrolizumab or atezolizumab + chemotherapy\n  2. cohort B (HR-/HER2-, PD-L1-): chemotherapy\n  3. cohort C (HR+/HER2-): CDK4/6 inhibitor + endocrine therapy\n  4. cohort D (HER2+): chemotherapy + trastuzumab and pertuzumab\n* Presence of measurable disease according to Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) v.1.1 and/or Positron Emission Tomography Response Criteria in Solid Tumors (PERCIST) criteria\n* Able to provide full informed consent for the study\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Pre-existing severe psychiatric disorders or other conditions that could impair the ability to provide informed consent\n* Inability to complete questionnaires\n* Presence of another malignancy in the previous 3 years\n* Symptomatic brain metastases\n* Ongoing treatment with antidepressant and/or anxiolytic drugs","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":1000,"start":"2025-06-25","pcd":"2029-06","upd":"2026-06-17","sponsor":"European Institute of Oncology","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Gabriella Pravettoni, MD, PhD · +39 0257489731 · gabriella.pravettoni@ieo.it","Mara Negri · +39 0257489536 · mara.negri@ieo.it"],"sites":[{"f":"Ospedali Riuniti di Ancona","city":"Ancona","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":43.6072,"lon":13.5103,"c":"Rossana Berardi"},{"f":"CRO (Centro di Riferimento Oncologico)","city":"Aviano","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":46.0706,"lon":12.5947,"c":"Fabio Puglisi, MD"},{"f":"Azienda Usl Toscana centro - Ospedale Santa Maria Annunziata","city":"Bagno a Ripoli","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":43.7512,"lon":11.3225,"c":"Carlotta Bacci, MD"},{"f":"IRCCS Istituto Tumori Giovanni Paolo II","city":"Bari","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":41.1207,"lon":16.8698,"c":"Nicola Silvestris, MD"},{"f":"ASST Papa Giovanni XXIII","city":"Bergamo","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.696,"lon":9.6672,"c":"Alberto Zambelli, MD"},{"f":"ASST Spedali Civili","city":"Brescia","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.5356,"lon":10.2147,"c":"Rebecca Pedersini, MD"},{"f":"Ospedale A. Perrino","city":"Brindisi","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":40.6322,"lon":17.9361,"c":"Saverio Cinieri, MD"},{"f":"ASST della Valle Olona","city":"Busto Arsizio","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.6113,"lon":8.8491,"c":"Maria Marconi, MD"},{"f":"Ospedale Valduce","city":"Como","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.8082,"lon":9.0832,"c":"Giovanni Scognamiglio, MD"},{"f":"Ospedale Careggi","city":"Florence","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":43.7792,"lon":11.2463,"c":"Icro Meattini, MD"},{"f":"Ospedale Policlinico San Martino","city":"Genova","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.216,"lon":11.8721,"c":"Lucia Del Mastro, MD"},{"f":"AOU Gaetano Martino di Messina","city":"Messina","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":38.1939,"lon":15.5526,"c":"Massimilano Berretta, MD"},{"f":"European Institute of Oncology","city":"Milan","pr":"","zip":"20141","s":"R","lat":45.4643,"lon":9.1895,"c":"Gabriella Pravettoni, MD"},{"f":"ASST Fatebenefratelli 